---
description: >
  Expand provisionBrain from two planning steps to four by adding playbook hub
  template and vault CLAUDE.md as independently idempotent InitStep items.
intent: >
  Expand provisionBrain from two planning steps (vault directories, MCP) to
  four (vault directories, playbook hub template, vault CLAUDE.md, MCP),
  with per-file idempotency and content templates as string literals, then
  update applySteps to handle brain-category file steps alongside the
  existing brain directory step.
---

## Plan

### 1. Update applySteps to handle brain-category file steps

The current `applySteps` handler assumes every `category: "brain"` step
with content carries a JSON array of directory names. The new playbook hub
and vault CLAUDE.md steps are also `category: "brain"` (for agent-facing
grouping) but carry Markdown content destined for a specific file path.
Without this change, applySteps would attempt `JSON.parse` on Markdown and
crash.

- [x] In `src/tools/init/applySteps/index.ts`, modify the brain-category
  branch (currently lines 50-61) to distinguish directory steps from file
  steps. The discriminant: if `filePath` has a file extension (use
  `path.extname`), treat it as a regular file write (mkdir parent, write
  content to filePath). If no extension, treat it as the existing directory
  scaffolding logic (JSON.parse content as directory array). This keeps the
  category as "brain" for both sub-types while routing them through
  different write paths.
- [x] Update the JSDoc on `applySteps` to document the new brain file step
  path alongside the existing brain directory step path.
- [x] Add tests in `src/tools/init/applySteps/index.test.ts` (create if it
  does not exist) covering: (a) a brain step with a `.md` filePath writes
  content as a file, (b) a brain step without an extension still creates
  directories from JSON content, (c) a brain step with `"exists"` status
  passes through unchanged.

### 2. Add the playbook hub template to provisionBrain

The spec requires a coding-playbook hub template as its own InitStep with
independent idempotency. The template must contain the exact section
structure the study-playbook skill expects but no fabricated content.

- [x] 2a. In `src/tools/init/provisionBrain/index.ts`, add a
  `PLAYBOOK_HUB_TEMPLATE` string constant containing the Markdown template.
  The template must have these five sections in order: `## Task Routing`
  (a Markdown table with the header row `| Task domain | Section |` and the
  separator row, but zero data rows), `## How to Use This Index`
  (navigation instructions explaining the hub-to-section-hub-to-child-note
  flow — keep it generic, no project-specific references),
  `## Always Read First` (two numbered placeholder lines for conventions
  and folder structure notes, using `[[wikilink]]` syntax with empty
  targets the user will fill in), `## Sections` (an empty numbered list
  placeholder), and `## Contents` (an empty flat list placeholder). Use the
  user's actual playbook hub at `coding-playbook/coding-playbook.md` (read
  during step 6 of the instructions) as the structural reference — match
  its heading order and section purpose, not its content.
- [x] 2b. Add a `buildPlaybookHubStep` async function. It takes
  `brainPath: string`, computes the target file path as
  `join(brainPath, "coding-playbook", "coding-playbook.md")`, checks
  existence with the existing `exists()` helper, and returns an InitStep
  with `name: "Playbook hub"`, `category: "brain"`, `filePath` pointing to
  the computed path, `status: "exists"` when the file is present or
  `status: "would-create"` with `content` set to the template when absent.
- [x] 2c. Wire `buildPlaybookHubStep` into the orchestrator function.
  Insert its call between `buildVaultStep` and the MCP step. The returned
  step goes into the array at position index 1 (after vault directories,
  before vault CLAUDE.md).

### 3. Add the vault CLAUDE.md template to provisionBrain

The spec requires a vault-root CLAUDE.md as its own InitStep with
independent idempotency. The template is scoped to vault navigation only.

- [x] 3a. In `src/tools/init/provisionBrain/index.ts`, add a
  `VAULT_CLAUDE_MD_TEMPLATE` string constant containing the Markdown
  template. The template must cover four concerns: (1) **Wikilink crawling
  protocol** — hub notes vs content notes, depth counting rules, never
  re-read, stay in scope. (2) **Decision protocol** — coding conventions
  route through the study-playbook skill, everything else through
  search_notes. (3) **Where to find things** — a Markdown table mapping
  information types to vault paths (coding conventions -> study-playbook
  skill, project context -> projects/, session logs -> journal/log/,
  research -> research/, tasks -> kanban/). (4) **Brain's role in AIDE** —
  a brief paragraph explaining that the vault is the pipeline's durable
  memory for research, retros, and conventions. Use the user's global
  CLAUDE.md (the "Your Brain" and "Decision Protocol" sections) as the
  structural reference for tone and scope. The template must NOT contain
  project-specific instructions, user preferences, business context, RTK
  instructions, or environment details.
- [x] 3b. Add a `buildVaultClaudeMdStep` async function. It takes
  `brainPath: string`, computes the target file path as
  `join(brainPath, "CLAUDE.md")`, checks existence, and returns an
  InitStep with `name: "Vault CLAUDE.md"`, `category: "brain"`, the
  computed filePath, and the template as content when absent.
- [x] 3c. Wire `buildVaultClaudeMdStep` into the orchestrator function.
  Insert its call after the playbook hub step and before the MCP step. The
  returned step goes into the array at position index 2 (after playbook
  hub, before MCP).

